# THE PLAYER'S SHELF -- what is on it when the game starts, and WHY each row is.
#
# Columns:  id | tier | amount | phase | note
#
#   id       a `data/catalog/compounds/*.psv` compound id, and nothing else. A
#            shelf row is a real species with a real molecular graph, because a
#            stock is a `VesselState` (GAME_DESIGN.md section 1) and a bag of
#            nouns cannot be charged into a flask.
#   tier     natural | intermediate | bottle -- see below. THE WHOLE POINT OF
#            THIS COLUMN IS THAT THE SHELF CAN SHRINK.
#   amount   mol of the FORMULA UNIT, sized for one bench experiment in a 1 L
#            flask rather than for a stockroom. Gases are small on purpose:
#            0.05 mol is about 1.2 L at room conditions, and 1 mol of gas in a
#            1 L flask is 24 bar.
#   phase    liquid | gas | solid -- where the charge lands. DECLARED, not
#            derived, and `tools/build_shelf.py` reports every row where the
#            engine's own estimate disagrees. It disagrees about olive oil by
#            550 K.
#   note     where a player gets it, in one clause.
#
# ## THE THREE TIERS, AND THEY ARE MEASURED RATHER THAN CHOSEN
#
#   natural       out of the ground, out of the air, or pressed out of something
#                 living. `tools/build_playable.py`'s NATURAL dict is the
#                 declaration, and it is the one hand judgement in that file.
#   intermediate  a route in `data/catalog` MAKES it, and that route is itself
#                 stranded. EARNABLE: the day a session makes its route
#                 reachable, the row is DELETED and the player earns it instead.
#   bottle        nothing in 173 catalog routes makes it at all. Bought, or the
#                 corpus grows a route.
#
# Measured by `validation/playable_levers.py` panel 3: granting the 24
# intermediate and 4 bottle species takes playable routes from 21 to 41, with no
# new chemistry of any kind. That is the cheapest distance on the board by a
# factor of four, and it is why this file exists before any more templates do.
#
# ## FOUR THINGS THIS FILE IS NOT
#
# IT IS NOT A PRICE LIST. Every priced species in the corpus -- 1167 of 1583 --
# is reachable through the picker's all-priced toggle, which is a separate axis
# and NOT a fourth tier. This file is only what a new player starts with.
#
# IT IS NOT FILTERED BY WHAT THE ENGINE CAN PRICE, and that is deliberate. SEVEN
# natural rows are REFUSED a price by the element floor -- gold, quartz, pyrite,
# pyrrhotite, pyrolusite, borax and cryolite. They stay, because "you can dig
# this up" is a true statement about the world whatever the estimators say, the
# picker greys them WITH THE REASON (GAME_DESIGN.md 8.3), and the day one of
# them is curated the row lights up with no edit here.
#
# TWO NATURAL SPECIES ARE MISSING AND CANNOT BE ADDED: `coal-marker` and
# `collagen-marker`. A marker has no molecular graph -- it is a rock, a mixture
# or a protein carried so the catalog's routes stay balanced -- so it cannot be
# a `VesselState`, and GAME_DESIGN.md 8.6 forbids a shelf entry that is not one.
# 45 natural species, 43 rows. The generator refuses an id it cannot resolve.
#
# GAME_DESIGN.md 8.5's example rows illustrate the FORMAT and not the CONTENT:
# `sulfuric-acid` is not natural. C1's route makes it from pyrite, and putting
# it here would delete the first route the game has.
#
# ## HOW A ROW BECOMES A CHARGE (`tools/build_shelf.py` resolves it, once)
#
# A mineral with a `mineral_data` lattice is charged AS THE LATTICE -- one solid
# species, not its ions -- because the lattice is the species that calcines,
# roasts and reduces, and it is also the one that dissolves: precipitation is
# priced lattice <-> ions through a Ksp (rock salt comes out at 6.09 mol/L
# against a measured 6.15). The two representations of CaCO3 are different
# species that do not know about each other, so choosing wrong would have cost
# either the kiln or the solution.
#
# A salt with NO lattice record is charged as its dissolved IONS, and its phase
# says `liquid` for that reason -- there is no crystal of it in this engine.
# --- NATURAL: 43 rows. Out of the ground, the air, or something living.
water                      | natural      | 5     | liquid | rain, a river, the sea
oxygen                     | natural      | 0.05  | gas    | air, 21%
nitrogen                   | natural      | 0.2   | gas    | air, 78%
carbon-dioxide             | natural      | 0.05  | gas    | air, and every fire
sulfur-s8                  | natural      | 0.2   | solid  | native sulfur, Sicilian or salt-dome
carbon-graphite            | natural      | 1     | solid  | graphite, or charcoal from wood
gold                       | natural      | 0.05  | solid  | native metal, panned
silver                     | natural      | 0.1   | solid  | native metal
sodium-chloride            | natural      | 1     | solid  | rock salt, or evaporated brine
calcium-carbonate          | natural      | 1     | solid  | limestone, chalk, shell
silicon-dioxide            | natural      | 1     | solid  | sand, quartz, flint
iron-iii-oxide             | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | haematite ore
aluminium-oxide            | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | bauxite
calcium-fluoride           | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | fluorspar
cryolite                   | natural      | 0.2   | solid  | Ivigtut cryolite, mined until 1987
copper-sulfide             | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | covellite ore
lead-sulfide               | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | galena ore
zinc-sulfide               | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | sphalerite ore
iron-disulfide             | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | pyrite, fool's gold
iron-ii-sulfide            | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | pyrrhotite
mercury-sulfide            | natural      | 0.2   | solid  | cinnabar ore
potassium-nitrate          | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | saltpetre from a nitre bed or a cave floor
sodium-nitrate             | natural      | 0.5   | liquid | Chile saltpetre, caliche -- dissolved: no lattice record
calcium-phosphate          | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | phosphate rock, and bone ash
calcium-sulfate            | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | anhydrite
gypsum                     | natural      | 0.5   | liquid | gypsum rock -- dissolved: the dihydrate has no lattice, anhydrite is the crystal
magnesium-carbonate        | natural      | 0.5   | liquid | magnesite -- dissolved: no lattice record
iron-ii-sulfate            | natural      | 0.3   | solid  | melanterite -- green vitriol weathers out of pyrite
manganese-dioxide          | natural      | 0.3   | solid  | pyrolusite
borax                      | natural      | 0.3   | solid  | tincal, from a dry lake bed
sucrose                    | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | cane or beet
glucose                    | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | grape sugar, honey
starch-unit                | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | grain, potato
cellulose-unit             | natural      | 0.5   | solid  | cotton, wood pulp
triolein                   | natural      | 0.2   | liquid | olive oil -- and the engine's own Tm for it is 829 K, which is 550 K wrong
oleic-acid                 | natural      | 0.3   | liquid | tallow, olive oil
tannic-acid-core           | natural      | 0.1   | solid  | oak gall, chestnut
indican                    | natural      | 0.1   | solid  | woad, the indigo plant
salicin                    | natural      | 0.2   | solid  | willow bark
eugenol                    | natural      | 0.3   | liquid | clove oil
alpha-pinene               | natural      | 0.3   | liquid | turpentine from pine resin
citronellal                | natural      | 0.3   | liquid | citronella oil
lignin-monomer-coniferyl   | natural      | 0.2   | solid  | wood lignin

# --- INTERMEDIATE: 24 rows. A stranded route makes each of these, so
# every one of them is EARNABLE and this block is meant to get shorter.
acrylonitrile              | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: propylene ammoxidation, itself stranded
aluminium                  | intermediate | 0.3   | solid  | chain: Hall-Heroult
aniline                    | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: nitrobenzene reduced
aspirin                    | intermediate | 0.2   | solid  | chain: salicylic acid acetylated
chloral                    | intermediate | 0.2   | liquid | chain: ethanol chlorinated
chlorobenzene              | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: benzene chlorinated
cobalt                     | intermediate | 0.05  | solid  | chain: a catalyst metal nothing in the corpus smelts
copper-ii-ion              | intermediate | 0.1   | liquid | chain: dissolved copper -- it IS an ion, there is no lattice to charge
copper-ii-oxide            | intermediate | 0.3   | solid  | chain: roasted copper ore
ethylene                   | intermediate | 0.05  | gas    | chain: a cracker product
glycerol                   | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: a fat saponified
hydrogen-chloride          | intermediate | 0.05  | gas    | chain: salt and vitriol
hydrogen-sulfide           | intermediate | 0.05  | gas    | chain: acid on a metal sulfide
iodomethane                | intermediate | 0.2   | liquid | chain: methanol and hydriodic acid
iron                       | intermediate | 0.5   | solid  | chain: the blast furnace
methane                    | intermediate | 0.05  | gas    | chain: a cracker product -- natural gas is DELIBERATELY not natural
nickel                     | intermediate | 0.05  | solid  | chain: a catalyst metal nothing in the corpus smelts
nitrobenzene               | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: benzene nitrated
nitrogen-dioxide           | intermediate | 0.02  | gas    | chain: the lead chamber's NOx carrier -- 0.5 mmol makes 40 mmol of acid
palladium                  | intermediate | 0.02  | solid  | chain: a catalyst metal nothing in the corpus smelts
phenol                     | intermediate | 0.3   | solid  | chain: cumene, or a fused benzenesulfonate -- and it MELTS at 314 K
propylene                  | intermediate | 0.05  | gas    | chain: a cracker product
sodium-acetate             | intermediate | 0.3   | liquid | chain: soda and vinegar -- dissolved: no lattice record
xylose                     | intermediate | 0.3   | solid  | chain: hemicellulose hydrolysed

# --- BOTTLE: 4 rows. NOTHING in 173 routes makes any of these, and they
# are worth only +1 route together, because each of those routes is short
# of something else as well. A reagent catalogue, not a work order.
benzaldehyde               | bottle       | 0.3   | liquid | bought: no route in the corpus makes it
malonic-acid               | bottle       | 0.2   | solid  | bought: no route in the corpus makes it
4-nitrophenol              | bottle       | 0.2   | solid  | bought: no route in the corpus makes it
bromoethane                | bottle       | 0.3   | liquid | bought: no route in the corpus makes it
